<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
<Document>
  <name>Wednesday Kyoto · May 27</name>
  <description><![CDATA[Southern Higashiyama walking tour · Gion Tanto okonomiyaki dinner]]></description>

  <Style id="locked"><IconStyle><scale>1.3</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/ylw-stars.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style>
  <Style id="major"><IconStyle><scale>1.1</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/red-circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style>
  <Style id="bonus"><IconStyle><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/blu-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style>
  <Style id="station"><IconStyle><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/rail.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style>

  <Folder>
    <name>LOCKED — confirmed bookings / hard anchors</name>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Shinkansen Nozomi 117 (Tokyo → Kyoto)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>07:00 depart → 09:12 arrive Kyoto</b><br><br><b>BOOKING:</b> ✅ Reservation 2005 · Green Car · Car 10, Seats 12-C + 12-D · D side = Fuji-side · window ~07:35-08:00<br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> Nozomi 117 N700 16-car set, Tokyo → Kyoto direct. Green Car: 2+2 seating, attendant service, hot oshibori, power outlets, in-car Wi-Fi (login: shinkansen-free-wifi).<br><br><b>WHY FOR YOU:</b> 12-D is the Mt. Fuji window seat. ~07:35-08:00 between Shin-Yokohama and Shizuoka, weather-pending Fuji visibility.<br><br><b>KNOWN FOR:</b> Premier Tokaido service; N700 rotating seats so you always face forward.<br><br>Address: Tokyo Station Tokaido Shinkansen platforms (south end)<br><br><b>↪ From hotel: leave 06:00 sharp</b>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#locked</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>139.7671,35.6812,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>

    <Placemark>
      <name>Ritz-Carlton Kyoto</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Bag drop 09:50 AM · check-in 15:00 (or earlier via Your24)</b><br><br><b>BOOKING:</b> ✅ Confirmation 90261043 · Corner Suite MINAMI · King · River view · Ambassador Elite<br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> Hotel on the Kamogawa river at Nijo-Ohashi. Kerry Hill Architects building, low-rise, river-facing rooms. Drop bags AM, do the temple walk, check in PM.<br><br><b>WHY FOR YOU:</b> Walking distance to Gion, Pontocho, Kiyamachi. Taxi to Kiyomizu (south Higashiyama) ~12 min. Message Ambassador first thing AM for Your24 early check-in.<br><br><b>KNOWN FOR:</b> Pierre Hermé pâtisserie in the hotel; the Spa is excellent for late-night decompress.<br><br>Address: Kamogawa Nijo-Ohashi Hotori, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto 604-0902 · +81-75-7465555<br><br><b>↪ From Kyoto Station: taxi 15 min, ¥1,800-2,400</b>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#locked</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>135.77078,35.01428,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
  </Folder>

  <Folder>
    <name>MAJOR — the planned spine</name>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Kyoto Station Hachijo → Ritz taxi (09:30)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>09:30 taxi from Hachijo exit</b><br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> Off the Shinkansen, head to Hachijo (south) exit for the bigger taxi rank.<br><br><b>WHY FOR YOU:</b> Drop bags at Ritz, then taxi to Kiyomizu to start the temple walk before the crush.<br><br><b>↪ Follow Hachijo exit signs from Shinkansen platform</b>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#major</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>135.7588,34.9858,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>

    <Placemark>
      <name>Kiyomizu-dera (清水寺)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>~10:30 arrive · ¥500 entry · grounds 06:00-18:00 · 60-90 min</b><br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> 778 CE Buddhist temple perched on a Higashiyama hillside, with the famous wooden stage projecting over the valley. UNESCO World Heritage 1994.<br><br><b>WHY FOR YOU:</b> THE iconic southern Higashiyama temple. The wooden-stage view over Kyoto is the canonical photo. Start of the day's walking spine — gravity assist DOWN from here through the slopes to Gion.<br><br><b>KNOWN FOR:</b> The wooden stage (13m above the slope, 168 zelkova pillars, no nails); Otowa Waterfall three streams; UNESCO World Heritage.<br><br>Address: 1-294 Kiyomizu, Higashiyama-ku<br><br><b>↪ Taxi from Ritz ~12 min, ¥1,200-1,500. Don't try public transit — taxi is faster and cheaper for two.</b>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#major</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>135.78489,34.99483,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>

    <Placemark>
      <name>Sannenzaka + Ninenzaka (三年坂・二寧坂)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>12:00-12:45 · walk DOWN from Kiyomizu · ~45 min browsing pace · free</b><br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> Two preserved stone-stepped slopes descending from Kiyomizu, lined with 200-year-old wooden machiya converted to shops, cafes, and small inns. Designated National Preservation Districts.<br><br><b>WHY FOR YOU:</b> The most-photographed walking sequence in Kyoto, but easy to enjoy because you walk DOWNHILL through it. Browse pace, shop, soak up the Edo machiya architecture. Karolina's craft thread + your pre-war thread both fed.<br><br><b>KNOWN FOR:</b> Preserved Edo wooden machiya; the Yasaka Pagoda framing at the bottom of Yasaka-no-To slope; Edo-period stone steps polished smooth by centuries of foot traffic.<br><br><b>↪ Walk down from Kiyomizu — gravity assist. ~10 min through both slopes if you don't stop.</b>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#major</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>135.78061,34.99888,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>

    <Placemark>
      <name>Yasaka Pagoda (Hokan-ji 法観寺)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>~13:00 · pagoda viewable always from outside · interior occasionally open · 15 min</b><br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> 5-story pagoda from 1440, 46m tall — the only structure remaining from the original Hokan-ji temple complex (589 CE). One of the few medieval pagodas you can occasionally go INSIDE.<br><br><b>WHY FOR YOU:</b> The iconic Kyoto frame: pagoda + wooden houses + sloping street. The slope down from Yasaka-no-To is the canonical photo location.<br><br><b>KNOWN FOR:</b> 1440 construction; 46m tall; the iconic Kyoto photo backdrop; rare medieval interior access.<br><br><b>↪ 5 min walk from bottom of Sannenzaka, then continue 3 min to Kodai-ji</b>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#major</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>135.77949,34.99935,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>

    <Placemark>
      <name>Kodai-ji (高台寺) — Hideyoshi's widow's temple</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>~13:30 · ¥600 entry · 09:00-17:30 · 45-60 min</b><br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> Zen temple founded 1606 by Toyotomi Hideyoshi's widow Nene to memorialize her late warlord-husband. Famous for the bamboo grove, mossy garden, Rikyu tea houses, and Edo-era gold-leaf lacquerwork.<br><br><b>WHY FOR YOU:</b> The quiet contemplative one after the Sannenzaka crowds. Garden + tea-house architecture + serious Edo-era lacquer art in one ¥600 ticket. Less crowded than Kiyomizu by this hour.<br><br><b>KNOWN FOR:</b> Kodai-ji maki-e (gold-leaf lacquer); Sen no Rikyu tea houses; the bamboo grove; Hideyoshi's widow's memorial complex.<br><br>Address: 526 Shimokawara-cho, Higashiyama-ku<br><br><b>↪ 5 min walk from Yasaka Pagoda</b>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#major</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>135.78062,35.00007,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>

    <Placemark>
      <name>Maruyama Park + Yasaka Shrine (丸山公園・八坂神社)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>~15:00 · free · always open · 30-45 min</b><br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> Yasaka Shrine: 656 CE Shinto shrine, the spiritual center of Gion and home base of the Gion Matsuri festival. Maruyama Park behind = Kyoto's first public park (1886), home to the most-photographed weeping cherry tree in Kyoto.<br><br><b>WHY FOR YOU:</b> Quintessential Gion-side shrine that locals actually use. The vermillion red main hall + the calm of Maruyama Park. May is leafy green, near-empty vs sakura season.<br><br><b>KNOWN FOR:</b> Gion Matsuri origin shrine; the weeping cherry tree (Gion no Yozakura); 1886 first-public-park status.<br><br><b>↪ Walk from Kodai-ji, 5-8 min through Maruyama Park</b>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#major</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>135.77852,35.00351,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>

    <Placemark>
      <name>Kennin-ji (建仁寺) — Kyoto's oldest Zen temple</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>~16:00 · ¥600 entry · 10:00-16:30 (last entry 16:00) · 45 min</b><br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> Founded 1202 by Eisai, the monk who brought Zen Buddhism AND TEA SEEDS from China to Japan. Kyoto's OLDEST Zen temple; one of the Kyoto Five Mountains.<br><br><b>WHY FOR YOU:</b> Zen temple with serious art collection (Twin Dragons ceiling + Wind/Thunder God National Treasure screens), and the birthplace of Japanese tea culture. Quieter than Kiyomizu by mid-afternoon. The walking-tour finale before dinner.<br><br><b>KNOWN FOR:</b> Eisai's lineage (the monk who brought tea from China in 1191); the Twin Dragons ceiling (2002); Wind God + Thunder God screens (early 17th century, National Treasures).<br><br>Address: 584 Komatsucho, Higashiyama-ku<br><br><b>↪ 10 min walk south from Yasaka Shrine through Gion's southern edge</b>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#major</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>135.77277,35.00057,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>

    <Placemark>
      <name>Gion Tanto (祇園たんと) — DINNER okonomiyaki + chuhai</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Wed DINNER ONLY 16:30-21:30 LO 21:30 · closed Thu · walk-in · cash/cc</b><br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> Kyoto-style okonomiyaki + iron-plate dishes + chuhai. Small neighborhood teppan counter on Shirakawa Canal near Tatsumi Bridge, Gion edge. Locals + repeat visitors, not the tourist-burned-out Hanamikoji crowd.<br><br><b>WHY FOR YOU:</b> Fluffy-yet-substantial Kyoto okonomiyaki, fresh lemon sours, no-frills setup — the right register after a walking day. ✓ Verified open Wed (closed only Thursdays).<br><br><b>KNOWN FOR:</b> Kyoto-style okonomiyaki (fuwafuwa fluffy with dashi notes); fresh lemon sours and chuhai; teppan iron-plate items.<br><br>Address: 京都府京都市東山区清本町372 (Higashiyama-ku, Kiyomotocho 372)<br><br><b>↪ ~12 min walk from Ritz south along Kamogawa then into Gion. Gion-Shijo Station ~3-5 min.</b>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#major</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>135.7745,35.00455,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>

    <Placemark>
      <name>Ritz-Carlton Kyoto (HOME end of night)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>~22:00+ home</b><br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> Walk back along Kamogawa from Gion ~12 min, or short taxi.<br><br><b>↪ From Gion Tanto: walk Kamogawa promenade north to Nijo-Ohashi ~12 min</b>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#major</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>135.77078,35.01428,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
  </Folder>

  <Folder>
    <name>BONUS — discovery zone</name>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Okonomiyaki Kiraku 三条本店 (dinner alt — locals-heavy)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Wed 11:30-13:40 LO · 17:00-22:00 LO · closed Mondays</b><br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> Long-time local favorite Kyoto okonomiyaki + teppan, casual neighborhood izakaya energy. Regulars, no spectacle. Fresh chuhai/lemon sours. Alt to Gion Tanto if you want the hidden-alley locals-heavy version.<br><br>Address: 京都府京都市東山区三条通白川橋東4丁目中之町208<br><br><b>↪ ~15 min walk east from Ritz · 5 min from Higashiyama subway</b>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#bonus</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>135.779,35.00833,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>

    <Placemark>
      <name>Shokudo Endo (食堂エンドウ) — LUNCH near Kiyomizu</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Wed 11:30-15:00 lunch only · 10-seat counter · phone before walking up</b><br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> Hidden-gem local cafeteria off Sannenzaka. Excellent maguro (tuna) donburi and seafood bowls, unfussy, generous portions. Cash-friendly. Praised by Japanese visitors for value and quality.<br><br>Address: 京都市東山区清水2-241-4 · Phone 075-525-5752<br><br><b>↪ 10-15 min walk from Kiyomizu through Sannenzaka side paths</b>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#bonus</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>135.782,34.997,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>

    <Placemark>
      <name>Gion Tempura Ramen KIRAKU (葵洛)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Wed 11:00-15:00 LO + 17:30-21:00 LO · daily</b><br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> Tempura + ramen combo counter in a machiya, opened May 2025. Convenient walkable lunch ramen for the Higashiyama day.<br><br>Address: 京都市東山区新橋通大和大路東入林下町434-2<br><br><b>↪ ~10 min walk from Ritz · 2 min from Gion-Shijo station</b>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#bonus</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>135.7758,35.0042,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>

    <Placemark>
      <name>Ramen Nishiki Sui</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Wed 11:00-14:30 + 18:00-21:00 LO 20:30 · closed Mondays</b><br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> Cozy ramen counter in the Shirakawa alley cluster. Creative Kyoto-style or matcha ramen (opened Nov 2025 — novelty risk, ask staff what's the actual house style on the day).<br><br>Address: 京都市東山区清本町375-4 末吉町一番路地 (alley off Kiyomotocho)<br><br><b>↪ ~12 min walk from Ritz · 348m from Gion-Shijo station · 100m from Gion Tanto — pick one or the other, not both same night</b>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#bonus</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>135.774,35.004,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>

    <Placemark>
      <name>Ramen Miyako Gion Honten (らぁ～めん京)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Wed 11:00-22:00 LO 21:30 (Fri/Sat to 03:00) · walk-in · no fixed closure</b><br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> Counter ramen, chicken/pork double broth. Reliable late-night Gion option — if Gion Tanto fills up or you want a late-night second meal after dinner.<br><br>Address: 京都市東山区祇園町北側303 1F<br><br><b>↪ ~14 min walk from Ritz</b>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#bonus</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>135.77773,35.00456,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>

    <Placemark>
      <name>Izakaya Yawaragi (居酒屋 和～やわらぎ～)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Wed 11:00-14:00 LO 13:30 + 17:00-24:00 LO 23:30</b><br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> Hidden obanzai (Kyoto small plates) counter near Higashiyama Station. Locals-dominant, deep sake list, chuhai available. Great as post-dinner drinks-and-snacks or alt to dinner if you want small plates instead of okonomiyaki.<br><br>Address: 京都市東山区東大路三条下ル東入南側 セゾン東山1F<br><br><b>↪ ~17 min walk from Ritz · 1 min from Higashiyama subway station</b>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#bonus</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>135.779,35.007,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>

    <Placemark>
      <name>Gion Tachinomi Yamaneko (山根子) — standing bar</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Daily 13:00-23:00 · walk-in · standing + high chairs</b><br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> 150-year-old machiya converted to a tachinomi standing bar. 50+ Kyoto sake selections + 8 craft beers on tap. Mixed crowd (craft-beer-tourist-friendly but locals too).<br><br>Address: 京都市東山区祇園町北側321-1<br><br><b>↪ ~13 min walk from Ritz · 200m from Gion Tanto</b>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#bonus</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>135.778,35.004,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>

    <Placemark>
      <name>Gion Shinbashi Takoyagi (祇園 新橋 たこやぎ) — late takoyaki</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>18:00-03:00 · closed Sundays · cash typical</b><br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> Takoyaki + okonomiyaki, evening-focused, opened mid-2025. 2F walk-up. Small, locals-leaning. Late-night option if you want octopus balls + beer at 23:00. NOTE: 100m from Gion Tanto — don't double up the okonomiyaki same night.<br><br>Address: 京都市東山区橋本町401 八百平ビル2F<br><br><b>↪ Same Gion cluster as Tanto</b>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#bonus</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>135.7747,35.005,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
  </Folder>

  <Folder>
    <name>STATIONS — transit hubs</name>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Tokyo Station (Tokaido Shinkansen)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Depart 07:00 · arrive by 06:40</b><br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> Tokaido Shinkansen platforms south end of Tokyo Station.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#station</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>139.7671,35.6812,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>

    <Placemark>
      <name>Kyoto Station (Hachijo exit)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Arrive 09:12 · taxi rank south side</b><br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> Hachijo (south) side for bigger taxi rank. To Ritz: 15 min, ¥1,800-2,400.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#station</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>135.7588,34.9858,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>

    <Placemark>
      <name>Gion-Shijo (Keihan line)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Gion area transit</b><br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> Closest station to Yasaka Shrine, Kennin-ji, Gion dining cluster. Walking distance from Ritz ~10 min.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#station</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>135.77272,35.00343,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>

    <Placemark>
      <name>Higashiyama (Tozai subway)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Closer for Okonomiyaki Kiraku Sanjo + Izakaya Yawaragi</b><br><br><b>WHAT IT IS:</b> Tozai subway. 5 min walk from Okonomiyaki Kiraku; 1 min from Yawaragi.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#station</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>135.7809,35.01054,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
  </Folder>

